  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{4}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})-2{cos}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}){sin}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})+{sin}^{4}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})-2{cos}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}){sin}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})+{sin}^{4}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}) & ={({cos}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={67.5}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {67.5}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({135}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({67.5}^{\u2218}))}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
